[agent] ### How the FTI ran on-platform
[agent] - Input CSVs uploaded to HopsFS; the job read them, engineered features, and wrote FG `airq963ee7` (Hudi upsert on `date`, materialization awaited).
[agent] - Feature view `airqtd963ee7` created over the FG; `create_train_test_split` materialized the versioned training dataset.
[agent] - XGBoost trained/evaluated on the split (metrics from the 188-row holdout), then refit on all history for the final forecast, and registered to the model registry.
[agent] - Forecast rows scored in-job; results written to online+offline FG `airqpred963ee7`.
[agent] ### Two CLI read-path quirks (interface notes, not deliverable problems)
[agent] - `hops td list airqtd963ee7` errors with `'FeatureView' object has no attribute '_get_training_dataset_schema'` — a client/backend version mismatch (CLI ships hsfs 5.1.0.dev1 against a 5.0.0 backend). The TD itself exists and was read back successfully inside the job.
[agent] - `hops sql` failed with a urllib3/proxy connection error; `hops fg preview` (via the Query Service) works and confirmed the 90 predictions.
[agent] One robustness fix was needed mid-run: `fs.get_feature_view`/`create_feature_view` returned `None` on this build, so I re-fetch the FV by name after creating it.
